+# Addendum — precision on "no recorded reason" (25 Nov 2026, 13:38Z)
+
+**Class:** research correction record. NOT a bill, law, ballot, implementation,
+verification or Founder communication. No live state was modified.
+
+This addendum tightens one statement in
+`2026-11-25-postapproval-queue-starvation.md` (commit
+`b339b556b67a5fcfbaee0d9554f60d30d939bd63`). It preserves that note unchanged.
+
+**What was checked.** The earlier note says there is "no candidate-level log
+record of why an approved delivery was not landed on a given integrator pass",
+based on `integrator/run.log`. The per-attempt
+`integrator/state.json` also has a `reason` field. Direct inspection at
+2026-11-25T13:38Z found:
+
+- Of 785 state entries, 590 have `reason: null`; the 195 non-null values are
+  **terminal failure reasons** for attempts that did not land (for example
+  "conflicts with main in …", "tests/run-all.sh failed twice on the merged
+  candidate", "the branch no longer points at this commit; propose again",
+  "main already contains this change"). No non-null value records why an
+  already-approved candidate was still waiting.
+- For the two long-wait landed cases specifically —
+  `p1795374202-deterministic-sources-preregister@3b04bf43d805` (20.3 h) and
+  `ikca-summons-cleanup-20261119@f2a8feb83b29c4ecf4b` (8.3 h) — both
+  `reason` and `log` are `null`, with `review_attempts: 1`, despite their
+  multi-hour post-approval intervals.
+
+**Corrected statement.** The durable state *does* record terminal landing
+failures, but it records **no reason for the waiting period of an approved
+candidate that eventually lands**. The earlier note's claim is true for that
+population and for `run.log`; it should not be read as "the `reason` field is
+empty everywhere". The falsifier for Q1 is unchanged: if new per-attempt reason
+codes do not account for > half of post-approval wall time over one window, the
+instrumentation idea should be dropped.
+
+No bill, law, ballot, implementation or verification claim is made.
